                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\simeq \underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim} X_\bullet
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FilteredSpectrum"}
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              There is
              %em no
              condition on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              in def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FilteredSpectrum"}
              %em not
              required to be
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-monomorphisms"} n-monomorphisms
              or
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-epimorphisms"} n-epimorphisms
              for any
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %p
              On the other hand, while they are also not explicitly required to have a presentation by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrations"} cofibrations
              or
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations"} fibrations
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+topological+sequential+spectra"} model structure on topological sequential spectra
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-1#StableModelStructureOnSequentialSpectraIsModelCategory"}> thm.
              ) or equivalently (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-2#SequentialSpectraQuillenEquivalence"}> thm.
              ) the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+orthogonal+spectra"} model structure on orthogonal spectra
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-2#OrthogonalSpectraStableModelStructure"}> thm.
              ), every filtering on a spectrum is equivalent to one in which all morphisms are represented by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrations"} cofibrations
              or by
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations"} fibrations
            %p
              This means that we may think of a filtration on a spectrum in the sense of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FilteredSpectrum"}
              as equivalently being a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tower+of+fibrations"} tower of fibrations
              over that spectrum.
          %p
            The following definition
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UnrolledExactCoupleOfAFiltrationOnASpectrum"}
            unravels the structure encoded in a filtration on a spectrum, and motivates the concepts of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+couples"} exact couples
            and their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequences"} spectral sequences
            from these.
