            %p
              Of all these abelian groups of order
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group"} cyclic group
              of order
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k= [k]
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^k
              for each
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          #PrimaryDecompositionGraphicalRepresentation.num_remark
            %h6#remark_12 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (graphical representation of
                = succeed "-primary" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %p
              Theorem
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FundamentalTheoremOfFinitelyGeneratedAbelianGroups"}
              says that for any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+number"} prime number
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-primary+group"} p-primary part
              of any finitely generated abelian group is determined uniquely up to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              by
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a total number
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in \mathbb{N}
                  of powers of
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition"} partition
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi k
                            %mn 1
                          %mo +
                          %msub
                            %mi k
                            %mn 2
                          %mo +
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo +
                          %msub
                            %mi k
                            %mi q
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = k_1 + k_2 + \cdots + k_q
            %p
              The corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-primary+group"} p-primary group
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munderover
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi q
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi k
                          %mi i
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underoverset{i = 1}{q}{\bigoplus} \mathbb{Z}/p^{k_i} \mathbb{Z}
                    \\,.
            %p
              In the context of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams+spectral+sequences"} Adams spectral sequences
              it is conventional to depict this information graphically by
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                  dots;
              %li
                %p
                  of which sequences of length
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi k
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_i
                  are connected by vertical lines, for
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo ,
                          %mi q
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in \{1, \cdots, q\}
            %p
              For example the graphical representation of the
              = succeed "-primary" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi p
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi p
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mn 3
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mn 4
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}
                    \\oplus
                    \\mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}
                    \\oplus
                    \\mathbb{Z}/p^3 \mathbb{Z}
                    \\oplus
                    \\mathbb{Z}/p^4\mathbb{Z}
            %p is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp;&amp; \bullet
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; &amp; \vert
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \bullet &amp; \bullet
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \vert &amp; \vert
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \bullet &amp; \bullet
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \vert &amp; \vert
                    \\\
                    \\bullet &amp; \bullet &amp; \bullet &amp; \bullet
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              This notation comes from the convention of drawing stable pages of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+spectral+sequence"} multiplicative
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams+spectral+sequences"} Adams spectral sequences
              and reading them as encoding the
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+S#ExtensionProblemForSpectralSequences"} extension problem
              for computing the homotopy groups that the spectral sequence converges to:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a dot at the top of a vertical sequence of dots denotes the group
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi p
                          %mi ℤ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}
              %li
                %p
                  inductively, a dot vetically below a sequence of dots denotes a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+extension"} group extension
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi p
                        %mi ℤ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}
                  by the group represented by the sequence of dots above;
              %li
                %p
                  a vertical line between two dots means that the generator of the group corresponding to the upper dot is, regarded after inclusion into the group extension, the product by
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                  of the generator of the group corresponding to the lower dot, regarded as represented by the generator of the group extension.
            %p So for instance
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\bullet
                    \\\
                    \\vert
                    \\\
                    \\bullet
                    }
            %p
              stands for an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              which forms a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+extension"} group extension
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi p
                            %mi ℤ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi p
                            %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow
                    \\\
                    A
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}
                    }
            %p
              such that multiplication by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              takes the generator of the bottom copy of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi p
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi p
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}
            %p
              This means that of the two possible choices of extensions (by example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TwoFiniteGroupsOfOrderp2"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              corresponds to the non-trivial extension
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo =
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mn 2
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = \mathbb{Z}/p^2\mathbb{Z}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi p
                            %mi ℤ
                          %mtd
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %msup
                              %mi p
                              %mn 2
                            %mi ℤ
                          %mtd
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi p
                            %mi ℤ
                          %mtd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z} &amp;
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\mathbb{Z}/p^2 \mathbb{Z} &amp;
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z} &amp;
                    }
            %p
              the image of the generator 1 of the first group in the middle group is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo =
                      %mi p
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = p \cdot 1
            %p Conversely, the notation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\bullet
                    \\\
                    \\\
                    \\bullet
                    }
            %p
              stands for an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              which forms a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+extension"} group extension
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi p
                            %mi ℤ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi p
                            %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow
                    \\\
                    A
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}
                    }
            %p
              such that multiplication by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              of the generator of the bottom group in the middle group does
              %em not
              yield the generator of the top group.
            %p
              This means that of the two possible choices (by example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TwoFiniteGroupsOfOrderp2"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              corresponds to the
              %em trivial
              extension
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo =
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi p
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi p
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = \mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z} \oplus \mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi p
                            %mi ℤ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi p
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo ⊕
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi p
                            %mi ℤ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi p
                            %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}
                    \\oplus
                    \\mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}
                    }
            %p
              the generator 1 of the bottom group lifts to the element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (0,1)
              in the middle group, and multiplication of that by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (0,0)
              instead of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,0)
            %p Similarly
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\bullet
                    \\\
                    \\vert
                    \\\
                    \\bullet
                    \\\
                    \\vert
                    \\\
                    \\bullet
                    }
            %p
              is to be read as the result of appending to the previous case a dot
              = succeed "," do
                %em below
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %msup
                              %mi p
                              %mn 2
                            %mi ℤ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi p
                            %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbb{Z}/p^2 \mathbb{Z}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow
                    \\\
                    A
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\mathbb{Z}/p \mathbb{Z}
                    }
            %p
              such that
              = succeed "-times" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo =
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mn 3
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = \mathbb{Z}/p^3 \mathbb{Z}
            %p And so on.
            %p
              For example the stable page of the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝔽
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_2
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+Adams+spectral+sequence"} classical Adams spectral sequence
              for computation of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-primary+group"} 2-primary part
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+groups+of+spheres"} stable homotopy groups of spheres
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                        %mo −
                        %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_{t-s}(\mathbb{S})
              has in (“internal”) degree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo −
                    %mi s
                    %mo ≤
                    %mn 13
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t-s \leq 13
              the following non-trivial entries:
            %p
              %img{:src => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/ClassicalAdamsSpectralSequence.jpg", :width => "600"}/
            %p
              (graphics taken from (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Symmetric+spectra"}> Schwede 12
              )))
            %p
              Ignoring here the diagonal lines (which denote multiplication by the element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h_1
              that encodes the additional
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
              structure on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo •
