                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %p
              Hence one direction of the claim is trivial. For the other direction we need to show that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [-,X]_\bullet
              to give an isomorphism on all
              = succeed "-equivalences" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
