          %h3#the_may_spectral_sequence The May spectral sequence
          %p
            The cobar complex (def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CobarComplex"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+Adams+spectral+sequence"} classical Adams spectral sequence
            (cor.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClassicalAdamsSpectralSequenceEstablished"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+cohomology"} cochain cohomology
            of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+complex"} cochain complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+complex"} filtration
            so that the induced
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence+of+a+filtered+complex"} spectral sequence of a filtered complex
            is computable and has trivial extension problem (
            %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+S#ExtensionProblemForSpectralSequences"}> rmk.
            ). This is called the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/May+spectral+sequence"} May spectral sequence
          %p
            We obtain this spectral sequence in prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MaySpectralSequenceForClassicalAdamsSpectralSequence"}
            below. First we need to consider some prerequisites.
          #CoModuleExtFromAToAForPrimitivelyGeneratedExteriorAlgebra.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_18 Lemma
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Gamma,A)
              be a graded commutative Hopf algebra, i.e. a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+commutative+Hopf+algebroid"} graded commutative Hopf algebroid
              with left and right unit coinciding for which the underlying
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
              is a free graded commutative
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{x_i\}_{i \in I}
            %p such that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  all generators
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_i
                  are
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/primitive+elements"} primitive elements
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  is in degree 0;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi deg
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi deg
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
