          %p And expanding the range yields this :
          %p
            %img{:alt => "stable homotopy groups of spheres at 2", :src => "http://www.math.cornell.edu/~hatcher/stemfigs/p%3D2pic.gif", :width => "800"}/
          %p
            (graphics taken from
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.cornell.edu/~hatcher/"} Hatcher’s website
          %h2#the_case__and_
            The case
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo =
                  %mi H
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = H \mathbb{F}_p
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %mi M
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = M U
          %p
            used to compute the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+groups"} stable homotopy groups
            of the complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M U
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology+of+MU"} homology of MU
          %p
            (hence, by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom%27s+theorem"} Thom's theorem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+ring"} cobordism ring
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                      %mi U
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo •
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega_\bullet^U \simeq \pi_\bullet U)
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+S#ThomTheorem"} Seminar session: Milnor-Quillen theorem on MU
          %p
            This is the
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Milnor-Quillen+theorem+on+MU"} Milnor-Quillen theorem on MU
            %em
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+S#QuillenTheoremOnMU"} Seminar session: Milnor-Quillen theorem on MU
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+S#Adams74"}> Adams 74, part II, around section 8
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+S#Lurie10"} Lurie 10, around lecture 9
          %h2#AdamsNovikovSpectralSequence
            Adams-Novikov spectral sequence (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo =
                  %mi M
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = M U
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %mi 𝕊
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = \mathbb{S}
          %p
            this is the classical
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams-Novikov+spectral+sequence"} Adams-Novikov spectral sequence
            , converges faster than the classical choice
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo =
                  %mi H
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = H \mathbb{F}_p
            to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+groups+of+spheres"} stable homotopy groups of spheres
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Kochman96"}> Kochman 96, section 5
            )
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %hr/
          %h2#References References
          %p For the general theory we follow the original
          %ul
            %li#Adams69
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Frank+Adams"}> John Frank Adams
                , section 2 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lectures on generalised cohomology
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Hilton"} Peter Hilton
                (ed.)
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Category Theory, Homology Theory and Their Applications III
            %li#Adams74
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Adams"}> Frank Adams
                , section III.15 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stable+homotopy+and+generalized+homology"} Stable homotopy and generalized homology
            %li#Bousfield79
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aldridge+Bousfield"}> Aldridge Bousfield
                , sections 5 and 6 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The localization of spectra with respect to homology
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.uio.no/studier/emner/matnat/math/MAT9580/v12/undervisningsmateriale/bousfield-topology-1979.pdf"} pdf
          %p For the homological algebra of comodules over Hopf algebroids we follow appendix A of
          %ul
            %li#Ravenel86
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Doug+Ravenel"}> Doug Ravenel
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Complex+cobordism+and+stable+homotopy+groups+of+spheres"} Complex cobordism and stable homotopy groups of spheres
          %p
            For the special case of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+Adams+spectral+sequence"} classical Adams spectral sequence
            and of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams-Novikov+spectral+sequence"} Adams-Novikov spectral sequence
            we follow
          %ul
            %li#Kochman96
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stanley+Kochman"}> Stanley Kochman
              , chapter 5 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bordism%2C+Stable+Homotopy+and+Adams+Spectral+Sequences"} Bordism, Stable Homotopy and Adams Spectral Sequences
